	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9706"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=146" title="View the profile of simplee">simplee</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 138<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/devil1.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								smoked again................    ranger down!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=146"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9706#msg9706"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9706#msg9706">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #13 on:</b> August 03, 2004, 03:06:14 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Zoning in before the healer was ready probably wasn&#039;t the best idea... but I have more issues with the ranger then anyone (since the paladin is obviously an ebay&#039;d player).<br /><br />As a ranger, he should have been doing any number of things that it didn&#039;t seem like he was doing... he could have root parked mobs on the pull (as they came into camp), he could have off-tanked, or he could have helped the druid heal.  Sure ranger heals aren&#039;t much, but if the druid is oom, or even low, every bit helps, and since the &quot;tank&quot; had so few HP, a ranger heal would have healed him 10%.  Plus, he would get healing aggro, giving the druid a chance to sit and med.<br /><br />And for the love of all things holy, what the hell was the wizard doing following the puller?!?
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Huntress Simplee Mee<br />69 Forest Stalker
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9707"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=744" title="View the profile of zigak">zigak</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 13<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=744"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9707#msg9707"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9707#msg9707">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #14 on:</b> August 03, 2004, 03:07:23 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I find it a lot more disturbing the wiz felt the need to follow the puller.&nbsp; Since you seem to know him, why did he do that?&nbsp; He must have had a reason.&nbsp; Even the noob paladin (I love noobs) knew not to follow the puller.</div><br />In defense of the wizard (I can&#039;t fucking believe I&#039;m defending my rant victim), I think his heart was in the right place, even if he was a raging asshat.&nbsp; I think he was going to attempt to root extra mobs or something...hell fucked if I know I don&#039;t read minds.&nbsp; The first time he followed, saw me fade, then drop invis he just turned tail and ran back to camp so I&#039;m not sure what he was thinking.&nbsp; The second time he may have wanted to prevent another overpull, but unwittingly would have been the cause of one if he didn&#039;t realise bards have a FD like ability.&nbsp; The ranger was just a straight no skill ass cheese. <br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />Making mistakes is one thing, apathy is another.&nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
